{{!
    @template tool_lp/progress_bar

    A progress bar with its sentence and its percentage, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors tool_lp/progress_bar of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500), admin/tool/lp/templates/progress_bar.mustache.
    Re-diff it against that file on every core upgrade: plan_page, course_competency_statistics and
    template_statistics call it as a parent with the three blocks progresstext, percentage and
    percentlabel, so the block names are its interface.

    Kept from core: the three blocks and their context fallbacks, and a native progress element with
    value and max="100" (no style attribute carries the number).
    Changed: the percentlabel block, which core declares and never prints, is printed beside the
    sentence; a label wrapping both names the bar, where core only described it through
    aria-describedby="progress-<uniqid>". That id is dropped: uniqid is one value per render, so
    template_statistics, which draws up to three bars, repeated it and pointed every bar at the first
    sentence. Nothing in core reads it. The classes are the theme's (scss/competency.scss).

    Context variables required for this template:
    * progresstextvalue A brief text that describes the progress bar.
    * percentagevalue The numeric value for the progress bar's percentage.
    * percentlabelvalue The progress bar's label that shows the percentage value.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "progresstextvalue": "3 out of 4 competencies are proficient",
        "percentagevalue": "75",
        "percentlabelvalue": "75.0 %"
    }
}}
<label class="dim-comp-progress">
    <span class="dim-comp-progress__head">
        <span class="dim-comp-progress__text">{{$progresstext}}{{progresstextvalue}}{{/progresstext}}</span>
        <span class="dim-comp-progress__value">{{$percentlabel}}{{percentlabelvalue}}{{/percentlabel}}</span>
    </span>
    <progress class="dim-comp-progress__bar" value="{{$percentage}}{{percentagevalue}}{{/percentage}}" max="100"></progress>
</label>
